        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Employees electing compensatory time in lieu of pay may accumulate a maximum of 240 hours. Employees whose accumulation is over 240 hours as of December 1, 1993, shall have their compensatory bank frozen at the amount of compensatory time in their banks as of December 1, 1993. Employees who have 240 hours or more of compensatory time in their banks must be paid for all overtime worked.",
